From 6e6e9dfc99289a772bf4d102bc7af2ac890e4eda Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 21:28:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(build): unbreak the GLSL gate; one phase timeline instead
 of three

The shaderpack gate was failing in all nine define variants: final.fsh declared
fractalPhase() with a fifth `vec3 baseColor` parameter that its body never read,
while the one call site passed four arguments. glslang has no matching overload
for that, so ci/build.sh's shimcheck step (a hard gate -- its else branch exits 1)
stopped the build before javac ever ran. Removed the unused parameter, which is
also what its 4-arg siblings lavaHellscapePhase / iceVoidPhase / spaceNebulaPhase
declare. shimcheck: 165/174 -> 174/174.

Separately, the storm ran on three different phase timelines. ci/palette_tables.py
is the declared single source of truth (TEAL_TO_PURPLE 5.10-5.50, PURPLE_TO_ROSE
5.75-6.05, ROSE_TO_EMBER 7.00-8.05) and says the routing is "identical in sky.fsh,
position.fsh and McsmStormPhase.java" -- which it was, and nowhere else:

  StormPalettes.java        4.95/5.30/5.52/5.92, no ember stage
  McsmStormAtmosphere.java  5.00/5.50/5.50/6.00, no ember stage

Both are live (the first paints the base mod's fog/cloud/pulse, the second is what
StoryModeSkyTint asks for the sky tint). Because neither had an ember stage, their
last ramp finished at ~6.15 while sky.fsh kept easing to 8.05: for the final quarter
of the storm's arc every fog, cloud, pulse and sky-tint colour was frozen while the
shader above it kept moving.

- McsmPhaseTimeline: one Java home for the timeline. Its weights() expands the
  shader's nested mix into four coefficients that sum to exactly 1, so callers no
  longer normalise and the degenerate zero-total branch is gone.
- StormPalettes: delegates; gains the ember stage; fog now takes the traced horizon
  stops it sits under instead of a green that appears in no sheet; cloud deck now
  uses the four MCSM_CLOUD_* constants the shader ships rather than a different set
  of three. pulseColor's "1 - sum" early term was identically zero after
  normalisation, so PULSE_EARLY could only ever appear as a hard step below 4.95 --
  it is now faded by McsmPhaseTimeline.presence().
- McsmStormAtmosphere: delegates; gains the ember stage. Stage colours unchanged
  (they are the artist's frame extractions).
- palette_tables.check_routing(): fails the build if any Java file outside
  McsmPhaseTimeline states a phase window, or if either consumer stops delegating.
  Verified to fail on the pre-fix tree and pass on this one.

Frozen base-mod API surface preserved (StormPalettes EJECTA_* / starColor / strength
are linked by the decompiled base mod, where a missing member is a NoSuchFieldError
javac cannot catch). haloRingColor/haloUnderColor deliberately left as-is because
GROUND_TRUTH F.2 retired the surface they paint.

All local gates pass: shimcheck 174/174, palette_tables, check_phase_uniform 520/520,
trace_sky_sheets, make_still_strips, apply_stage_palette, sync_backdrop_palette,
measure_stills, iris_tu, split_p4_model, measure_hugeback, content textures, preflight.
